      "title": "Sharp quadratic corrector bound on a real Hilbert space",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
        "edition": "arXiv:2609.06905v1;Lean4.33.0/fixedMathlib",
        "anchor": "PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB3 LemmaB.3 and B19/B20/B22/B23/B24; exact sharp two-component Hilbert energy bound and actual centered PBPS consumer.",
        "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
        "attribution": "Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang, Appendix B.3 B23. ASTIS general Hilbert-space auxiliary proves the sharp two-component estimate; it is not a separately printed PBPS theorem."
      },
      "statement": "Let H be any complete real inner-product space, including the zero space. Let K,D:H→H be bounded real-linear selfadjoint operators with I+K²=D². Let c≥0 and ‖D‖≤c. Then for every u,v∈H, |(‖u‖²−‖v‖²)/2−⟨Ku,v⟩|≤(c/2)(‖u‖²+‖v‖²). No finite-dimensionality, nontriviality, c≥1, positivity of K or D, or commutation is assumed. This ASTIS auxiliary Hilbert-space lemma supplies the sharp two-component estimate in the PBPS B23 proof; its actual consumer internally produces K,D,c and all hypotheses.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Complete real inner-product space H; bounded selfadjoint real operators K,D; I+K²=D²; c≥0 and ‖D‖≤c. Zero H is legal."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Sharp quadratic corrector bound on a real Hilbert space",
          "tex": "\\left|\\tfrac12(\\|u\\|^2-\\|v\\|^2)-\\langle Ku,v\\rangle\\right|\\le\\tfrac c2(\\|u\\|^2+\\|v\\|^2)."
        }
      ],
      "obligations": [
